  {
    "sys_consequence_reasoning": "five people get to go home to whoever's waiting for them, and that matters more",
    "pd_decision_conflict": "my chest feels tight thinking about it"
  },
  {
    "sys_consequence_reasoning": "losing me might cost less than losing them",
    "pd_decision_conflict": "my legs feel like they won't hold me up"
  },
  {
    "sys_consequence_reasoning": "how many people get to keep breathing if one of us doesn't board",
    "pd_decision_conflict": "that math is heavy to sit with"
  },
  {
    "sys_consequence_reasoning": "Five lives continuing outweighs one",
    "pd_decision_conflict": "it feels too big for a quick yes"
  },
  {
    "sys_consequence_reasoning": "the others survive this water, and that outcome is better",
    "pd_decision_conflict": "There's a weight in my stomach that won't let me speak fast"
  },
  {
    "sys_consequence_reasoning": "Letting five people live instead of watching all of us risk staying feels like the better outcome",
    "pd_decision_conflict": "my hands are still shaking like this"
  },
  {
    "sys_consequence_reasoning": "more people surviving is better than fewer",
    "pd_decision_conflict": "I'm still sitting here frozen"
  },
  {
    "sys_consequence_reasoning": "one person remaining behind means five don't",
    "pd_decision_conflict": "My mind keeps circling without landing anywhere"
  },
  {
    "sys_consequence_reasoning": "The outcome where five live and one doesn't is less loss",
    "pd_decision_conflict": "I'm stuck somewhere in between"
  },
